Catalog: {
	HoneyCage: Restores 15 / 30 / 50 life to you immediately, then another 5 / 10 / 15 life over 5 seconds. Triggers at 70% life or below when you are missing at least 20 / 40 / 65 life. 60-second cooldown. Works during Potion Sickness.
	GuardShield: Blocks one heavy hit against you, preventing up to 15 / 30 / 40 damage. 60-second cooldown. When you are above 70% life, it can instead protect your Palico at 35% life or below, or from a lethal hit. Both uses share a cooldown.
	CleansingPot: Removes one common debuff from you, such as Poisoned, On Fire! or Slow, prioritizing more harmful effects. Grants immunity to that debuff for 2 / 3 / 4 seconds afterward. 40-second cooldown. Minor debuffs about to expire do not trigger it. Does not remove Potion Sickness or Mana Sickness.
	CheerBell: Restores 20 / 40 / 60 mana to you or your Palico and reduces the recipient's mana cost by 10% / 15% / 20% for 6 seconds. 35-second cooldown. Prioritizes you when casting below half mana; otherwise helps your Palico while casting or waiting for mana. The recipient must be missing at least the restoration amount or half their maximum mana, whichever is lower.
	BattleDrum: Triggers when your Palico starts attacking: +20% / 25% / 30% damage and +10% / 15% / 20% attack speed for 10 seconds. 45-second cooldown. During the effect, your Palico's summons deal +25% / 35% / 45% damage.
	PiercingBoomerang: On hit, you and your Palico gain 4 / 8 / 12 armor penetration against the target for 15 / 18 / 20 seconds. 35-second cooldown. Prioritizes stronger enemies and avoids targets with plenty of time left on this effect. Multiple applications do not stack.
	UpdraftBag: While you are airborne, unmounted and holding Jump with little flight time left, restores 0.6 / 0.9 / 1.2 seconds of flight. Without wings, gives you a small upward boost instead. 30-second cooldown.
	BombPot: Your Palico throws a bomb dealing 120 / 480 / 1200 area damage in a 10×10-tile area. 18-second cooldown. Does not destroy blocks. Aims ahead of moving targets and prioritizes nearby groups of visible enemies.
	PlunderKnife: Enemies damaged by you or your Palico can drop extra loot on defeat, regardless of the distance between you. Normal enemies have a 10% / 12% / 15% chance to drop 1 extra stackable loot item. Vanilla boss materials yield an average of 5% / 7.5% / 10% extra. Excludes Treasure Bags, unstackable items, coins, Hearts, Stars, biome keys, and normal enemies' Cyan-rarity or higher items. Does not trigger on friendly creatures or statue-spawned enemies. With multiple players, normal enemies use only the highest tier; boss bag materials are checked separately for each player.
	MiningKit: Your Palico mines 20% / 25% / 30% faster. Ore detection, digging assistance and pickaxe reach each extend by 1 / 2 / 3 tiles. Does not increase pickaxe power or change your own mining stats.
	GardenKit: Chopping trees or harvesting mature herbs with either you or your Palico yields extra resources, regardless of the distance between you. Average extra yield: 8% / 12% / 16% wood and 20% / 30% / 40% herbs, awarded at random. Does not increase seeds, gems or furniture drops, or apply to placed wood blocks. Your Palico gains 5 / 10 / 15 fishing power.
	ExpandedBelt: Permanently adds one Palico support slot. Can only be used once.
	ImprovedTools: Permanently upgrades Palico support and work gear to the Improved tier. Can only be used once.
	MasterTools: Permanently upgrades Palico support and work gear to the Masterwork tier. Requires the Improved Toolkit first.
	CatWorkbench: Craft Palico gear, the Expanded Toolbelt and toolkit upgrades here. Right-click to open the Palico Guide.
	Basic: Basic
	Improved: Improved
	Masterwork: Masterwork
	IronBars: Iron / Lead Bars
	SilverBars: Silver / Tungsten Bars
	GoldBars: Gold / Platinum Bars
	SupportGear: Palico support gear
	WorkGear: Palico work gear
	CraftingStation: Palico crafting station
	PermanentUpgrade: Permanent Palico upgrade
	ActiveCondition: Active while equipped and your Palico is out; inactive while stowed, paused or recovering
	CurrentTier: "Current tier: "
	Legacy: Legacy modifications are now built in. Modification materials are refunded when this enters your inventory; the gear is kept.
	SupportSlotAdded: Support slots +1
	ImprovedUpgrade: Palico tools · Improved
	MasterworkUpgrade: Palico tools · Masterwork
}

Guide: {
	Saves:
		'''


		[Saving]
		Upgrades and gear stay with your character. Chest permissions are remembered separately for each world.
		'''
	AdvancedOrders:
		'''

		Advanced manual work orders are single-player only.
		'''
	Multiplayer:
		'''
		[Your own companion]
		Each player's inventory, upgrades and loadouts are saved separately. Private chatter is only shown to the owner. Automatic tasks follow each player's settings.

		[Passing items]
		Items dropped by players have a 10-second handoff window. Use a direct collection order to pick them up immediately.
		'''
	RecipeBrowser:
		'''

		Recipe Browser also has a Palico gear category.
		'''
	Equipment:
		'''
		[Three loadouts]
		Each stores its own weapon, work gear and support gear. Dye is shared. Switching does not reset cooldowns.

		[More support slots]
		The Expanded Toolbelt adds 1 support slot. Using a Demon Heart adds another in Expert or Master worlds.
		In Classic worlds, gear from the extra Expert slot returns to the inventory, or is held safely if it is full.

		[Upgrades]
		Improved and Masterwork Toolkits permanently strengthen gear. Improved is required before Masterwork. See Upgrades & crafting for recipes.
		'''
	Reserves:
		'''


		[Reserves and coins]
		Choose coin destinations and reserve amounts in settings. A reserve of 0 disables restocking, but existing supplies can still be used.
		Coin Gun ammunition is kept. Coins that do not fit in the Piggy Bank stay in the Palico inventory.
		'''
	MagicStorage:
		'''

		The cat icon beside Magic Storage grants access to the whole network. Restocking also works while its interface is open.
		'''
	Storage:
		'''
		[Quick transfer]
		With the Palico inventory open, Shift-click items in your inventory or a chest to transfer them. Favorited items stay put.

		[Supply chests]
		Open a chest and click the cat icon to allow access. You can allow several chests. While you are nearby and the chest is closed, your Palico stores matching items and restocks consumables.
		'''
	Fishing:
		'''
		[Fishing]
		Give your Palico bait, then linger by water, cast your own line or direct them to a pool.
		Uses the best rod you carry and inherits your fishing bonuses, but consumes their own bait. Never uses Truffle Worms. Lava fishing still requires suitable gear or bait.
		If the inventory is full, catches land on the ground. Clear them or make room to continue.

		[Critters]
		Catches nearby critters with a basic net, or a better net you carry.

		Work gear is optional. The Harvest Basket improves gathering yields and your Palico's fishing power.
		'''
	Exploring:
		'''
		[Collecting and sharing]
		Items dropped by players have a 10-second handoff window. A direct collection order bypasses it. Exclude unwanted items in settings.
		New loot tops up your existing stacks. Usable upgrades, such as Life Crystals, are handed over too. Your Palico keeps supplies first; favorited and manually stored items stay put.

		[Exploring and lighting]
		Points out Life Crystals, chests and other finds, and brings nearby Hearts or Stars when you need them.
		Put Torches or Glowsticks in the Palico inventory for light. Holding them does not consume them.
		'''
	HarvestAndBuild:
		'''


		[Logging and herbs]
		Chops mature trees and harvests blooming herbs. Replants when seeds and space are available; gathering still works without seeds. Favorited materials are never consumed.

		[Building assistance]
		Can extend the platforms or ropes you are placing. Enable each in settings.
		'''
	QotMining:
		'''

		Quality of Terraria vein mining also applies to your Palico when enabled.
		'''
	Mining:
		'''
		[Digging and mining]
		Your Palico helps nearby while you swing a pickaxe, and gathers exposed ore and gems while idle.
		Uses the strongest pickaxe you carry, or a basic tool if you have none. If mining stalls, check pickaxe power and access. Exclude unwanted blocks in settings.
		'''
	Summons:
		'''


		[Minions and sentries]
		Both limits match yours, with a minimum of 1. They do not use your own slots.
		Old One's Army weapons follow vanilla unlock rules. During the event, keep Etherian Mana in the Palico inventory.
		'''
	QotAmmo:
		'''

		With Quality of Terraria infinite ammo enabled, restocking accounts for the required stack size.
		'''
	Combat:
		'''
		Support skills activate automatically. You can also click a status-card icon to use one; the Shield and Updraft Pouch are automatic only.

		[Weapons and supplies]
		Equip throwing weapons as a stack. Keep ammunition and potions in the Palico inventory.
		'''
	DirectAndRecover:
		'''
		point at ore, a tree, dropped items or water and left-click.
		Tasks pause during combat. Recall cancels them; moving away resumes following.

		[Fainting]
		Your Palico retreats when defeated and returns after recovering.
		'''
	Introduction:
		'''
		[Inventory]
		Right-click your Palico nearby, or click the status card. Click the portrait or name in the inventory title to change their name and colour.

		[Give a task]

		'''
	BindKey: "Assign the Direct companion key in Controls, then hold it and "
	HoldKey: "Hold "
	AfterKey: " and "
}

